      "risk_48h": null,
      "risk_7d": null,
      "next_update": null,
      "raw_text": "(2) AN AREA OF CONVECTION (INVEST 90W) HAS PERSISTED NEAR 12.5N \n156.6E, APPROXIMATELY 416 NM NORTHEAST OF CHUUK. ANIMATED ENHANCED \nINFRARED IMAGERY (EIR) DEPICTS A BROAD AREA OF CYCLONIC ROTATION \nSITUATED ON A WEST-TO-EAST ORIENTED TROUGH, WITH CYCLING DEEP \nCONVECTION ALONG THE SOUTHERN AND EASTERN PERIPHERY. ENVIRONMENTAL \nCONDITIONS ARE MOSTLY FAVORABLE WITH WARM (28-29C) SEA SURFACE \nTEMPERATURES, GOOD POLEWARD OUTFLOW, LOW TO MODERATE (15-20KT) \nVERTICAL WIND SHEAR, AND DRY AIR TO THE NORTH. GLOBAL MODELS ARE IN \nAGREEMENT THAT THE INVEST 90W WILL SLOWLY CONSOLIDATE OVER THE NEXT \n36-48 HOURS AND TRACK GENERALLY NORTH-NORTHWESTWARD AS THE CONVECTION \nAND WINDS BUILD. MAXIMUM SUSTAINED SURFACE WINDS ARE ESTIMATED AT 13 \nTO 18 KNOTS. MINIMUM SEA LEVEL PRESSURE IS ESTIMATED TO BE NEAR 1007 \nMB. THE POTENTIAL FOR THE DEVELOPMENT OF A SIGNIFICANT TROPICAL \nCYCLONE WITHIN THE NEXT 24 HOURS IS LOW.",
