      "raw_text": "Central and Western East Pacific (EP97):\nShowers and thunderstorms associated with an area of low pressure \nlocated several hundred miles southwest of the southwestern coast \nof Mexico have become a little less organized this morning. \nEnvironmental conditions appear conducive for development, however, \nand a tropical depression is expected to form during the next couple \nof days while it moves generally west-northwestward to westward over \nthe central and western portions of the eastern Pacific basin. For \nmore information, including gale warnings, please see the High Seas \nForecast issued by the National Weather Service. \n* Formation chance through 48 hours...high...80 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...90 percent.",
